Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: fsl_sai: publish driver data before requesting IRQ

A pending SAI interrupt during a kexec handover can invoke fsl_sai_isr
as soon as devm_request_irq succeeds. Its regmap callbacks obtain sai
through dev_get_drvdata; publishing it later produces a NULL dereference
in fsl_sai_readable_reg. Set it after initializing soc_data, before
regmap creation and IRQ registration.

--- a/sound/soc/fsl/fsl_sai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/fsl/fsl_sai.c
@@ -1418,6 +1418,7 @@
 
 	sai->pdev = pdev;
 	sai->soc_data = of_device_get_match_data(dev);
+	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, sai);
 
 	sai->is_lsb_first = of_property_read_bool(np, "lsb-first");
 
@@ -1547,7 +1548,6 @@
 
 	sai->pinctrl = devm_pinctrl_get(&pdev->dev);
 
-	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, sai);
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
 	if (!pm_runtime_enabled(dev)) {
 		ret = fsl_sai_runtime_resume(dev);
